    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the roster as our premier play, boasting an elite 81.87 efficiency score. Facing a favorable matchup against the right-handed Brown, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a strong platoon advantage and the optimal leadoff spot, making him our highest-ceiling asset for Roto category production. Joining him at the top of the performance chart is **Sam Antonacci** (67.67), whose leadoff assignment against Yesavage is bolstered by a significant SP skill edge. Additionally, the middle infield duo of **Nasim Nunez** (67.37) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (66.11) represents a high-floor stack against the vulnerable Lopez, as both players leverage high-value park factors to elevate their scoring well above their baseline projections.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Curtis Mead**, who nearly cracked the lineup with a 58.98 score. While **Curtis Mead** would have benefited from the same high-scoring matchup against Lopez that boosted **Nasim Nunez** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, his efficiency fell just shy of our starting threshold when the optimizer prioritized the positional flexibility and park-adjusted ceilings of our current utility starters. Meanwhile, caution is advised regarding **Jackson Merrill**; despite a solid 54.45 score, a 38% rain risk introduces a layer of volatility that could affect his availability or rhythm. While **Kyle Tucker** (53.63) and **Andy Pages** (49.57) face a tough outing against the precision of Schlittler, their ability to contribute across the board\u2014particularly **Kyle Tucker**\u2014remains vital for maintaining our competitive standing in SB and HR, even if their raw efficiency scores are tempered by the opposing starter\u2019s skill.",
